Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Mirror the window menu in the macOS menu bar.

New Mac Driver option "NativeMenuBar" (per program via AppDefaults). When the key
window has a standard Win32 menu, its items are shown in the macOS menu bar between
the application menu and the Window menu. Each menu is refreshed right before it
opens (WM_INITMENU/WM_INITMENUPOPUP, 0.3 s timeout, falls back to the previous
contents), and choosing an item posts WM_COMMAND. Shortcuts from the item text
(e.g. "Ctrl+S") are displayed as macOS key equivalents (Ctrl -> Command) but are
not handled by the menu, so the program still processes the key exactly once.
The in-window menu bar is unchanged.

---
